      "problem": "Consider a function $f:{R}^{2\\times 3}\\to {R}^{2}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=A[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{a}_{12}}=${{field-1}}.",
